    "work_id": "anf-works/victorinus-on-the-creation-of-the-world",
    "canonical_ref": "Victorin.Fabr.s3",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "God produced that entire mass for the adornment of His majesty in six days; on the seventh to which He consecrated it . . . with a blessing.",
    "chunk_index": 2,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 290,
    "date_range": [
      260,
      304
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/victorinus-on-the-creation-of-the-world#Victorin.Fabr.s4",
    "work_id": "anf-works/victorinus-on-the-creation-of-the-world",
    "canonical_ref": "Victorin.Fabr.s4",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "For this reason, therefore, because in the septenary number of days both heavenly and earthly things are ordered, in place of the beginning I will consider of this seventh day after the principle of all matters pertaining to the number of seven;",
    "chunk_index": 3,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 290,
    "date_range": [
      260,
      304
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/victorinus-on-the-creation-of-the-world#Victorin.Fabr.s5",
    "work_id": "anf-works/victorinus-on-the-creation-of-the-world",
    "canonical_ref": "Victorin.Fabr.s5",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "and as far as I shall be able, I will endeavour to portray the day of the divine power to that consummation.",
    "chunk_index": 4,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 290,
    "date_range": [
      260,
      304
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/victorinus-on-the-creation-of-the-world#Victorin.Fabr.1.s1",
    "work_id": "anf-works/victorinus-on-the-creation-of-the-world",
    "canonical_ref": "Victorin.Fabr.1.s1",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "In the beginning God made the light, and divided it in the exact measure of twelve hours by day and by night, for this reason, doubtless, that day might bring over the night as an occasion of rest for men’s labours;",
    "chunk_index": 5,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 290,
    "date_range": [
      260,
      304
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/victorinus-on-the-creation-of-the-world#Victorin.Fabr.1.s2",
    "work_id": "anf-works/victorinus-on-the-creation-of-the-world",
    "canonical_ref": "Victorin.Fabr.1.s2",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "that, again, day might overcome, and thus that labour might be refreshed with this alternate change of rest, and that repose again might be tempered by the exercise of day.",
    "chunk_index": 6,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 290,
    "date_range": [
      260,
      304
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/victorinus-on-the-creation-of-the-world#Victorin.Fabr.1.s3",
    "work_id": "anf-works/victorinus-on-the-creation-of-the-world",
    "canonical_ref": "Victorin.Fabr.1.s3",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "“On the fourth day He made two lights in the heaven, the greater and the lesser, that the one might rule over the day,",
    "chunk_index": 7,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 290,
    "date_range": [
      260,
      304
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/victorinus-on-the-creation-of-the-world#Victorin.Fabr.1.s4",
    "work_id": "anf-works/victorinus-on-the-creation-of-the-world",
    "canonical_ref": "Victorin.Fabr.1.s4",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "the other over the night,”—the lights of the sun and moon and He placed the rest of the stars in heaven, that they might shine upon the earth, and by their positions distinguish the seasons, and years, and months, and days, and hours.",
    "chunk_index": 8,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 290,
    "date_range": [
      260,
      304
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/victorinus-on-the-creation-of-the-world#Victorin.Fabr.2.s1",
    "work_id": "anf-works/victorinus-on-the-creation-of-the-world",
    "canonical_ref": "Victorin.Fabr.2.s1",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Now is manifested the reason of the truth why the fourth day is called the Tetras, why we fast even to the ninth hour, or even to the evening, or why there should be a passing over even to the next day.",
    "chunk_index": 9,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 290,
    "date_range": [
      260,
      304
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/victorinus-on-the-creation-of-the-world#Victorin.Fabr.2.s2",
    "work_id": "anf-works/victorinus-on-the-creation-of-the-world",
    "canonical_ref": "Victorin.Fabr.2.s2",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Therefore this world of ours is composed of four elements—fire, water, heaven, earth. These four elements, therefore, form the quaternion of times or seasons.",
    "chunk_index": 10,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 290,
    "date_range": [
      260,
      304
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/victorinus-on-the-creation-of-the-world#Victorin.Fabr.2.s3",
    "work_id": "anf-works/victorinus-on-the-creation-of-the-world",
    "canonical_ref": "Victorin.Fabr.2.s3",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "The sun, also, and the moon constitute throughout the space of the year four seasons—of spring, summer, autumn, winter; and these seasons make a quaternion.",
    "chunk_index": 11,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 290,
    "date_range": [
      260,
      304
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/victorinus-on-the-creation-of-the-world#Victorin.Fabr.2.s4",
    "work_id": "anf-works/victorinus-on-the-creation-of-the-world",
    "canonical_ref": "Victorin.Fabr.2.s4",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "And to proceed further still from that principle, lo, there are four living creatures before God’s throne, four Gospels, four rivers flowing in paradise;",
    "chunk_index": 12,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 290,
    "date_range": [
      260,
      304
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/victorinus-on-the-creation-of-the-world#Victorin.Fabr.2.s5",
    "work_id": "anf-works/victorinus-on-the-creation-of-the-world",
    "canonical_ref": "Victorin.Fabr.2.s5",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "four generations of people from Adam to Noah, from Noah to Abraham, from Abraham to Moses, from Moses to Christ the Lord, the Son of God;",
    "chunk_index": 13,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 290,
    "date_range": [
      260,
      304
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/victorinus-on-the-creation-of-the-world#Victorin.Fabr.2.s6",
    "work_id": "anf-works/victorinus-on-the-creation-of-the-world",
    "canonical_ref": "Victorin.Fabr.2.s6",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "and four living creatures, viz., a man, a calf, a lion, an eagle; and four rivers, the Pison, the Gihon, the Tigris, and the Euphrates.",
    "chunk_index": 14,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 290,
    "date_range": [
      260,
      304
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/victorinus-on-the-creation-of-the-world#Victorin.Fabr.2.s7",
    "work_id": "anf-works/victorinus-on-the-creation-of-the-world",
    "canonical_ref": "Victorin.Fabr.2.s7",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "The man Christ Jesus, the originator of these things whereof we have above spoken, was taken prisoner by wicked hands, by a quaternion of soldiers.",
    "chunk_index": 15,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 290,
    "date_range": [
      260,
      304
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/victorinus-on-the-creation-of-the-world#Victorin.Fabr.2.s8",
    "work_id": "anf-works/victorinus-on-the-creation-of-the-world",
    "canonical_ref": "Victorin.Fabr.2.s8",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Therefore on account of His captivity by a quaternion, on account of the majesty of His works,—that the seasons also, wholesome to humanity,",
    "chunk_index": 16,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 290,
    "date_range": [
      260,
      304
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/victorinus-on-the-creation-of-the-world#Victorin.Fabr.2.s9",
    "work_id": "anf-works/victorinus-on-the-creation-of-the-world",
    "canonical_ref": "Victorin.Fabr.2.s9",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "joyful for the harvests, tranquil for the tempests, may roll on,—therefore we make the fourth day a station or a supernumerary fast.",
    "chunk_index": 17,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 290,
    "date_range": [
      260,
      304
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/victorinus-on-the-creation-of-the-world#Victorin.Fabr.3.s1",
    "work_id": "anf-works/victorinus-on-the-creation-of-the-world",
    "canonical_ref": "Victorin.Fabr.3.s1",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "On the fifth day the land and water brought forth their progenies. On the sixth day the things that were wanting were created;",
    "chunk_index": 18,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 290,
    "date_range": [
      260,
      304
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/victorinus-on-the-creation-of-the-world#Victorin.Fabr.3.s2",
    "work_id": "anf-works/victorinus-on-the-creation-of-the-world",
    "canonical_ref": "Victorin.Fabr.3.s2",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "and thus God raised up man from the soil, as lord of all the things which He created upon the earth and the water.",
    "chunk_index": 19,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 290,
    "date_range": [
      260,
      304
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/victorinus-on-the-creation-of-the-world#Victorin.Fabr.3.s3",
    "work_id": "anf-works/victorinus-on-the-creation-of-the-world",
    "canonical_ref": "Victorin.Fabr.3.s3",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Yet He created angels and archangels before He created man, placing spiritual beings before earthly ones. For light was made before sky and the earth.",
    "chunk_index": 20,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 290,
    "date_range": [
      260,
      304
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/victorinus-on-the-creation-of-the-world#Victorin.Fabr.3.s4",
    "work_id": "anf-works/victorinus-on-the-creation-of-the-world",
    "canonical_ref": "Victorin.Fabr.3.s4",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "This sixth day is called parasceve, that is to say, the preparation of the kingdom. For He perfected Adam, whom He made after His image and likeness.",
    "chunk_index": 21,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 290,
    "date_range": [
      260,
      304
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/victorinus-on-the-creation-of-the-world#Victorin.Fabr.3.s5",
    "work_id": "anf-works/victorinus-on-the-creation-of-the-world",
    "canonical_ref": "Victorin.Fabr.3.s5",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "But for this reason He completed His works before He created angels and fashioned man, lest perchance they should falsely assert that they had been His helpers.",
    "chunk_index": 22,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 290,
    "date_range": [
      260,
      304
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/victorinus-on-the-creation-of-the-world#Victorin.Fabr.3.s6",
    "work_id": "anf-works/victorinus-on-the-creation-of-the-world",
    "canonical_ref": "Victorin.Fabr.3.s6",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "On this day also, on account of the passion of the Lord Jesus Christ, we make either a station to God, or a fast.",
    "chunk_index": 23,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 290,
    "date_range": [
      260,
      304
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/victorinus-on-the-creation-of-the-world#Victorin.Fabr.3.s7",
    "work_id": "anf-works/victorinus-on-the-creation-of-the-world",
    "canonical_ref": "Victorin.Fabr.3.s7",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "On the seventh day He rested from all His works, and blessed it, and sanctified it. On the former day we are accustomed to fast rigorously, that on the Lord’s day we may go forth to our bread with giving of thanks.",
    "chunk_index": 24,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 290,
    "date_range": [
      260,
      304
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/victorinus-on-the-creation-of-the-world#Victorin.Fabr.3.s8",
    "work_id": "anf-works/victorinus-on-the-creation-of-the-world",
    "canonical_ref": "Victorin.Fabr.3.s8",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "And let the parasceve become a rigorous fast, lest we should appear to observe any Sabbath with the Jews, which Christ Himself, the Lord of the Sabbath, says by His prophets that “His soul hateth;”",
    "chunk_index": 25,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 290,
    "date_range": [
      260,
      304
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/victorinus-on-the-creation-of-the-world#Victorin.Fabr.3.s9",
    "work_id": "anf-works/victorinus-on-the-creation-of-the-world",
    "canonical_ref": "Victorin.Fabr.3.s9",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "which Sabbath He in His body abolished, although, nevertheless, He had formerly Himself commanded Moses that circumcision should not pass over the eighth day, which day very frequently happens on the Sabbath, as we read written in the Gospel.",
    "chunk_index": 26,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 290,
    "date_range": [
      260,
      304
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/victorinus-on-the-creation-of-the-world#Victorin.Fabr.3.s10",
    "work_id": "anf-works/victorinus-on-the-creation-of-the-world",
    "canonical_ref": "Victorin.Fabr.3.s10",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Moses, foreseeing the hardness of that people, on the Sabbath raised up his hands, therefore, and thus figuratively fastened himself to a cross.",
    "chunk_index": 27,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 290,
    "date_range": [
      260,
      304
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/victorinus-on-the-creation-of-the-world#Victorin.Fabr.3.s11",
    "work_id": "anf-works/victorinus-on-the-creation-of-the-world",
    "canonical_ref": "Victorin.Fabr.3.s11",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "And in the battle they were sought for by the foreigners on the Sabbath-day, that they might be taken captive, and, as if by the very strictness of the law, might be fashioned to the avoidance of its teaching.",
    "chunk_index": 28,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 290,
    "date_range": [
      260,
      304
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/victorinus-on-the-creation-of-the-world#Victorin.Fabr.4.s1",
    "work_id": "anf-works/victorinus-on-the-creation-of-the-world",
    "canonical_ref": "Victorin.Fabr.4.s1",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "And thus in the sixth Psalm for the eighth day, David asks the Lord that He would not rebuke him in His anger, nor judge him in His fury;",
    "chunk_index": 29,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 290,
    "date_range": [
      260,
      304
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/victorinus-on-the-creation-of-the-world#Victorin.Fabr.4.s2",
    "work_id": "anf-works/victorinus-on-the-creation-of-the-world",
    "canonical_ref": "Victorin.Fabr.4.s2",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "for this is indeed the eighth day of that future judgment, which will pass beyond the order of the sevenfold arrangement. Jesus also, the son of Nave, the successor of Moses, himself broke the Sabbath-day;",
    "chunk_index": 30,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 290,
    "date_range": [
      260,
      304
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/victorinus-on-the-creation-of-the-world#Victorin.Fabr.4.s3",
    "work_id": "anf-works/victorinus-on-the-creation-of-the-world",
    "canonical_ref": "Victorin.Fabr.4.s3",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "for on the Sabbath-day he commanded the children of Israel to go round the walls of the city of Jericho with trumpets, and declare war against the aliens.",
    "chunk_index": 31,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 290,
    "date_range": [
      260,
      304
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/victorinus-on-the-creation-of-the-world#Victorin.Fabr.4.s4",
    "work_id": "anf-works/victorinus-on-the-creation-of-the-world",
    "canonical_ref": "Victorin.Fabr.4.s4",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Matthias also, prince of Judah, broke the Sabbath; for he slew the prefect of Antiochus the king of Syria on the Sabbath, and subdued the foreigners by pursuing them.",
    "chunk_index": 32,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
